# Private, full laptop DB recovery dumps. Never serve or publish these files.
/.local-db-backups/
scripts/cache/
data/
# Generated, not authored. build/ holds solved rail profiles and the station /
# level-crossing extracts the scripts under scripts/ write; tmp/ is scratch.
# They were tracked by accident and had grown to 52 MB of JSON that nothing
# reads at runtime and the deploy explicitly keeps out of the docroot — every
# server checkout was pulling them for nothing. Regenerate with the
# scripts/build-*.mjs that produced them; the imported projects themselves live
# in the database.
build/
tmp/
recordings/
# Local playtest captures stay on disk; authored reports and recorder code ship.
docs/campaign-playtest-2026-09-05/
docs/campaign-playtest-2026-09-08/
docs/campaign-playtest-fixes-2026-09-08/*
!docs/campaign-playtest-fixes-2026-09-08/perf-recorder.mjs
!docs/campaign-playtest-fixes-2026-09-08/perf-summary.mjs
docs/campaign-presentation-fixes-2026-09-07/
docs/campaign-selected-integration-2026-09-07/
/foot.png
# Proposal fixtures dumped from a live consensus-builder backend for offline /
# deterministic walk-mode testing (?consensusApi=fixture). A whole named plan
# is ~300 files / 7 MB — regenerate by curling /proposals/<id>; the handful of
# small fixtures committed before this rule stay tracked (ignore is untracked-
# only) and keep working.
website/dev-proposal-fixtures/
# Machine-generated profiler captures, anywhere under performance/. The
# convention was already stated in performance/README.md ("Generated JSON and
# screenshots belong in performance/results/, which is intentionally ignored by
# git") and performance/results/.gitignore, but an archive directory outside
# results/ slipped 28,666 lines of capture JSON into the tree — enough to push
# the branch diff past what review tooling accepts. The measured NUMBERS belong
# in the decision record beside them; the raw payloads do not belong in git.
performance/**/*.json
# All of results/ is generated: bake-CLI snapshots and trial binaries, harness
# logs, screenshots. Ignore the directory itself rather than each run's naming
# scheme — listing them one by one let a new run kind through again (54 .log
# files under crowd-faces-2026-09-08-run2, beside 2.8 GB of captures).
performance/station3d/results/
!performance/station3d/scenarios.json
!performance/station3d/ground.scenarios.json
!performance/station3d/surface-audit.budget.json
!performance/station3d/paired.scenarios.json
!performance/station3d/*.summary.json
# Generated from pinned npm packages by build:station3d and shipped with the
# site. Keeping the copies out of git avoids maintaining vendored source twice.
website/vendor/
# Blender's automatic backup of the previous save (.blend1, .blend2, …) and the
# export logs a study run leaves beside its GLB; the .blend source is tracked.
*.blend[0-9]*
.*-export.log
